body:
It's possible to use a service worker script [like this](https://github.com/gzuidhof/coi-serviceworker/blob/master/coi-serviceworker.js) to register a service worker, then reload the page, and then intercept the document and add COEP/COOP headers (`require-corp`/`same-origin`). This is a hacky way to cross-origin isolate a page in situations where it otherwise wouldn't be possible (e.g. static sites where the developer doesn't control the server and thus can't add "actual" headers).

However, this hack doesn't seem to work with the new `credentialless` header. I'm wondering if there's anything in the spec that says this shouldn't work. Here are some minimal reproductions (only tested in Chrome/Chromium since I believe it's the only browser that supports `credentialless`):

* Setting headers with the **server** isolates the page, and the cross-origin image **is** displayed: https://coep-credentialless-with-server.glitch.me/ — ([view/edit code](https://glitch.com/edit/#!/coep-credentialless-with-server))
* Setting headers with **service worker** isolates the page, but cross-origin image **is not** displayed: https://coep-credentialless-with-serviceworker.glitch.me/ — ([view/edit code](https://glitch.com/edit/#!/coep-credentialless-with-serviceworker))

So the service worker approach seems to behave like `require-corp` instead of `credentialless`. Here's the image-loading error that I see in DevTools:

![The FetchEvent for url resulted in a network error response: Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy prevented from serving the response to the client.](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1167575/159747101-efd346ed-8f03-4487-adae-3fc452d439ac.png)

Code edit/view links are above, but for convenience, both documents look like the code below, except the service worker version loads the service worker script in the `<head>`. Not that I added a timeout before loading the image because there seemed to be some sort of race condition type thing happening where the image would load before the service worker had registered.
```html
<html>
  <head></head>
  <body>
    
    <div id="outputEl"></div>
    
    <script>
      console.log("crossOriginIsolated:", window.crossOriginIsolated);
      setTimeout(() => {
        outputEl.innerHTML = `<img src="https://via.placeholder.com/350x150">`;
      }, 1000);
    </script>
    
  </body>
</html>
```
Here's the code for the service worker ([link to file](https://coep-credentialless-with-serviceworker.glitch.me/coi-serviceworker.js)):
```js
// Edited version of: https://github.com/gzuidhof/coi-serviceworker - Guido Zuidhof, licensed under MIT
if(typeof window === 'undefined') {
  self.addEventListener("install", () => self.skipWaiting());
  self.addEventListener("activate", e => e.waitUntil(self.clients.claim()));

  async function handleFetch(request) {
    if(request.cache === "only-if-cached" && request.mode !== "same-origin") {
      return;
    }
    
    let r = await fetch(request).catch((e) => console.error(e));
    
    if(r.status === 0) {
      return r;
    }

    const headers = new Headers(r.headers);
    headers.set("Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy", "credentialless");
    headers.set("Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy", "same-origin");
    
    return new Response(r.body, { status: r.status, statusText: r.statusText, headers });
  }

  self.addEventListener("fetch", function(e) {
    e.respondWith(handleFetch(e.request));
  });
  
} else {
  (async function() {
    if(window.crossOriginIsolated !== false) return;

    let registration = await navigator.serviceWorker.register(window.document.currentScript.src).catch(e => console.error("COOP/COEP Service Worker failed to register:", e));
    if(registration) {
      console.log("COOP/COEP Service Worker registered", registration.scope);

      registration.addEventListener("updatefound", () => {
        console.log("Reloading page to make use of updated COOP/COEP Service Worker.");
        window.location.reload();
      });

      // If the registration is active, but it's not controlling the page
      if(registration.active && !navigator.serviceWorker.controller) {
        console.log("Reloading page to make use of COOP/COEP Service Worker.");
        window.location.reload();
      }
    }
  })();
}
```

There are no COOP/CORP/COEP/CORS headers in the response of [the image being requested](https://via.placeholder.com/350x150):
```
accept-ranges: bytes
alt-svc: h3=":443"; ma=86400, h3-29=":443"; ma=86400
cache-control: max-age=604800
content-length: 1253
content-type: image/png
date: Thu, 24 Mar 2022 14:51:15 GMT
expires: Thu, 31 Mar 2022 14:51:14 GMT
last-modified: Wed, 30 Dec 2020 01:00:11 GMT
```
